<title>TURKEY: Turk Otosan 96 profits more than triple.</title>
<headline>Turk Otosan 96 profits more than triple.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996 final results</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)   7,221.36  vs  1,975.16</p>
<p>    Net profit		    9,532.19  vs  2,607.22</p>
<p>    Net sales		    45,214.83  vs 17,665.82</p>
<p>    Operating profit	   10,875.65  vs  3,603.48</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	  3,391.11  vs    443.37</p>
<p>    Interest Paid		     9.91  vs	5.70</p>
<p>    Total debts		  11,100.37  vs  3,960.19</p>
<p>    Equity			 14,414.68  vs  5,262.67</p>
<p>    Capital			 1,320.00  vs  1,320.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Commercial vehicle and passenger car producer Otosan Otomobil Sanayi A.S. is owned 30 percent by Ford Motor Co and 53.9 percent by Turkey's leading industrial Koc group and Koc family.</p>
<p>The company plans to pay 10,027 lira cash dividend per 2,500 lira nominal valued share from its 1996 profits after approval at the annual meeting of shareholders and directors on March 27.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 84.9 percent wholesale inflation in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212-2750875 GUZ EKS</p>
</text>
